:: F1 {"position":"275,25","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: B: ATP

ATP is the immediate energy currency used to drive biosynthetic reactions, transport processes and mechanical work. ATP hydrolysis releases usable free energy. DNA and RNA are information-storage molecules, while glucose is a fuel that is metabolised to generate ATP rather than serving as the cell's direct energy currency.

