[[Next->Q2]]


:: F10 {"position":"25,275","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: C: Amylopectin – storage polysaccharide containing alpha(1→4) and alpha(1→6) linkages

Amylopectin is a branched storage polysaccharide containing alpha(1→4) chains and alpha(1→6) branch points. Glycogen is the principal animal storage polysaccharide, cellulose forms plant cell walls, and chitin functions structurally rather than as an ATP storage molecule.

