[[Summary]]


:: F2 {"position":"525,25","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: C: Brain

The brain consumes a large proportion of resting energy expenditure because neurons continuously maintain ion gradients and signalling activity. Brain tissue stores little fuel and depends on a steady nutrient supply. Skin, bone and adipose tissue generally have substantially lower immediate energy requirements.

