[[Next->Q3]]


:: F3 {"position":"775,25","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: B: It is the primary carbon source available to many cells

Glucose is a central metabolic substrate and a major carbon and energy source for many cell types. Cells can store excess glucose as glycogen, and glucose oxidation contributes significantly to ATP production. Therefore the statements that it is plant-specific, cannot be stored, or is uninvolved in ATP generation are incorrect.

