[[Next->Q4]]


:: F4 {"position":"1025,25","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: C: To drive Na+/K+-ATPase activity and solute reabsorption

Kidney function requires extensive active transport. Na+/K+-ATPases consume ATP to maintain ion gradients that drive reabsorption of salts, nutrients and water. Cellulose is not synthesised by human kidneys, oxygen is not stored there, and action potential generation is not the major explanation for its high ATP demand.

