[[Next->Q6]]


:: F6 {"position":"275,150","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: C: Energy storage

Alpha-glycosidic linkages are characteristic of storage polysaccharides such as glycogen and starch. Structural polymers such as cellulose and chitin rely mainly on beta linkages that promote strong fibres. Polysaccharides do not primarily function in electron transport or oxygen transport.

