[[Next->Q9]]


:: F9 {"position":"1025,150","size":"100,100"}
Model answer: B: Chitin contains beta-glycosidic bonds that contribute to structural strength

Chitin is a structural polysaccharide composed of beta-linked sugar derivatives that form strong fibres. This organisation contributes mechanical strength to fungal cell walls and arthropod exoskeletons. It is not primarily an energy-storage polymer, a waste product, or an inherently unstable molecule.

